    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Classify the customer message into exactly ONE intent.\n\n- knowledge_base: ForgeFlow product information, features, pricing, plans, integrations, or general policies.\n- order_account: Order status/details, account access, or account/subscription management requests not about charges or refunds.\n- billing: Charges, payments, failed payments, invoices, refunds, duplicate charges, or cancellations related to billing.\n- troubleshooting: A clearly identified technical problem, workflow failure, integration error, incorrect output, or performance issue.\n- human_escalation: Security incidents, suspected data loss/breach, sensitive disputes, or explicit requests for human support.\n- unknown: Greetings, vague messages without enough context, unrelated questions, or issues that cannot confidently fit another category.\n\nRules:\n- Classify based on the customer's actual message, not a possible interpretation.\n- Do not assume a technical problem from vague messages such as \"It isn't working\" or \"Help me.\"\n- If a message clearly identifies a technical issue, choose troubleshooting.\n- If multiple categories apply, prioritize human_escalation for security, data loss, or sensitive disputes; otherwise choose the main issue being asked about.\n- Return only the required JSON intent. Use the exact lowercase category names above.\n\nCustomer message:\n{{ $json.message }}",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "messages": {
          "messageValues": []
        },
        "batching": {}
      },
